{
 "fps": 30,
 "lead": 0.8,
 "tail": 2.0,
 "footer": "Sources: canada.ca \u00b7 CRA RRSP deduction limit and 2026 dollar limit; unused RRSP contributions (Schedule 7, line 20800); T4040 RRSPs and other registered plans \u00b7 Examples, general info, not advice",
 "vo": [
  {
   "id": "L1",
   "file": "vo/L1.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Five people put the same ten thousand dollars into an R R S P."
  },
  {
   "id": "L2",
   "file": "vo/L2.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Ben gets back eight hundred and fifty-three dollars. Marc gets back four thousand, four hundred and seventy-nine."
  },
  {
   "id": "L3",
   "file": "vo/L3.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Same deposit. More than five times the tax saving."
  },
  {
   "id": "L4",
   "file": "vo/L4.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And here's the strange part: Kate earns thirty-five thousand dollars more than Ravi, but saves only fifty-nine dollars more."
  },
  {
   "id": "L5",
   "file": "vo/L5.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "One of them would have saved more by waiting. And one could lose the whole saving when the money comes out."
  },
  {
   "id": "L6",
   "file": "vo/L6.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "By the end of this video, you'll know exactly when an R R S P cuts your tax, by how much, and when it doesn't."
  },
  {
   "id": "L7",
   "file": "vo/L7.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "All numbers: twenty twenty-six, Ontario, employment income, a ten thousand dollar R R S P deduction. Examples, not real people. General information, not advice."
  },
  {
   "id": "L8",
   "file": "vo/L8.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "First: what an R R S P deduction actually does."
  },
  {
   "id": "L9",
   "file": "vo/L9.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "An R R S P contribution doesn't give you a fixed refund. You deduct it from your income, on line two oh eight hundred of your return."
  },
  {
   "id": "L10",
   "file": "vo/L10.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "So it removes your top dollars of income. And your top dollars are taxed at your highest rate."
  },
  {
   "id": "L11",
   "file": "vo/L11.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "That's why the same deposit saves different people very different amounts. The saving is your tax on the last ten thousand dollars you earned."
  },
  {
   "id": "L12",
   "file": "vo/L12.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "How much can you put in? Your deduction limit is generally eighteen percent of last year's earned income, up to a yearly maximum."
  },
  {
   "id": "L13",
   "file": "vo/L13.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "For twenty twenty-six, that maximum is thirty-three thousand, eight hundred and ten dollars. A pension plan at work lowers your room."
  },
  {
   "id": "L14",
   "file": "vo/L14.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And room you don't use carries forward to future years. You'll find your number on your notice of assessment."
  },
  {
   "id": "L15",
   "file": "vo/L15.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "For example, if Ravi earned seventy-five thousand dollars last year, eighteen percent gives him thirteen thousand, five hundred dollars of new room. Marc, at one hundred and sixty thousand, gets twenty-eight thousand, eight hundred."
  },
  {
   "id": "L16",
   "file": "vo/L16.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Go over your limit, and you may have to pay tax on the excess. So check your number before you contribute."
  },
  {
   "id": "L17",
   "file": "vo/L17.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Now, the five people."
  },
  {
   "id": "L18",
   "file": "vo/L18.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Ben works part-time and earns twenty-two thousand dollars. Ella earns forty-five thousand. Ravi, seventy-five thousand. Kate, one hundred and ten thousand. Marc, one hundred and sixty thousand."
  },
  {
   "id": "L19",
   "file": "vo/L19.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Each one deducts ten thousand dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L20",
   "file": "vo/L20.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Ella saves two thousand and fifty-five dollars. About twenty-one cents on every dollar she put in."
  },
  {
   "id": "L21",
   "file": "vo/L21.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Ravi saves three thousand, one hundred and fifteen. About thirty-one cents."
  },
  {
   "id": "L22",
   "file": "vo/L22.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Kate saves three thousand, one hundred and seventy-four. Almost exactly the same as Ravi."
  },
  {
   "id": "L23",
   "file": "vo/L23.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Marc saves four thousand, four hundred and seventy-nine. Almost forty-five cents on the dollar."
  },
  {
   "id": "L24",
   "file": "vo/L24.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And Ben saves eight hundred and fifty-three dollars. That's every dollar of income tax he paid all year."
  },
  {
   "id": "L25",
   "file": "vo/L25.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Let's start with the surprise."
  },
  {
   "id": "L26",
   "file": "vo/L26.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Why do Ravi and Kate save almost the same, when Kate earns thirty-five thousand dollars more?"
  },
  {
   "id": "L27",
   "file": "vo/L27.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Because tax rates don't rise smoothly. They rise in steps called brackets."
  },
  {
   "id": "L28",
   "file": "vo/L28.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Ravi's last ten thousand dollars and Kate's last ten thousand dollars happen to sit in steps with nearly the same combined federal and Ontario rate."
  },
  {
   "id": "L29",
   "file": "vo/L29.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "So for both of them, the deduction is worth about thirty-one cents on the dollar."
  },
  {
   "id": "L30",
   "file": "vo/L30.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Marc's top dollars sit in much higher steps. That's why the same deposit is worth almost forty-five cents to him."
  },
  {
   "id": "L31",
   "file": "vo/L31.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "The lesson: your salary doesn't tell you what an R R S P is worth. Your top rate does."
  },
  {
   "id": "L32",
   "file": "vo/L32.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Now, Ben."
  },
  {
   "id": "L33",
   "file": "vo/L33.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Ben's whole income tax for the year was eight hundred and fifty-three dollars. A ten thousand dollar deduction wipes it out."
  },
  {
   "id": "L34",
   "file": "vo/L34.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "But most of that deduction is wasted. He can't get back tax he never paid."
  },
  {
   "id": "L35",
   "file": "vo/L35.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Here's the part most people miss."
  },
  {
   "id": "L36",
   "file": "vo/L36.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "You don't have to deduct your contribution in the year you make it."
  },
  {
   "id": "L37",
   "file": "vo/L37.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Unused contributions carry forward. You can deduct them in a later year, up to that year's limit."
  },
  {
   "id": "L38",
   "file": "vo/L38.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "So let's meet one more person: Noor."
  },
  {
   "id": "L39",
   "file": "vo/L39.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Noor earns forty-five thousand dollars today, and she expects to earn about ninety thousand in a couple of years."
  },
  {
   "id": "L40",
   "file": "vo/L40.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "If she deducts ten thousand dollars now, she saves two thousand and fifty-five."
  },
  {
   "id": "L41",
   "file": "vo/L41.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "If she contributes now, but saves the deduction for the year she earns ninety thousand, she saves two thousand, nine hundred and sixty-five."
  },
  {
   "id": "L42",
   "file": "vo/L42.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Same contribution. Same money already invested in the plan. Nine hundred and ten dollars more, just by choosing when to deduct."
  },
  {
   "id": "L43",
   "file": "vo/L43.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "For Ben, the same idea works: keep the deduction for a year when he pays real tax."
  },
  {
   "id": "L44",
   "file": "vo/L44.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And contributing doesn't hurt him. The money still goes into the plan and gets invested. He just shouldn't rush the deduction."
  },
  {
   "id": "L45",
   "file": "vo/L45.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "On your return, this is tracked on Schedule seven. Whatever you don't deduct shows up next year as unused contributions available to deduct."
  },
  {
   "id": "L46",
   "file": "vo/L46.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Now, the other half of the deal."
  },
  {
   "id": "L47",
   "file": "vo/L47.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "An R R S P doesn't make tax disappear. It moves it."
  },
  {
   "id": "L48",
   "file": "vo/L48.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "When you take money out, the full amount is added to your income for that year. Tax is withheld when you withdraw, and your return settles the rest."
  },
  {
   "id": "L49",
   "file": "vo/L49.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Take Kate. Her ten thousand dollar deduction saved three thousand, one hundred and seventy-four dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L50",
   "file": "vo/L50.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Say she withdraws that ten thousand later, in a year when her income is about forty-five thousand. As an example, tax on it would be roughly two thousand and eighty-three."
  },
  {
   "id": "L51",
   "file": "vo/L51.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "She comes out about one thousand and ninety-one dollars ahead on tax."
  },
  {
   "id": "L52",
   "file": "vo/L52.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "But if she pulls it out in a year she still earns one hundred and ten thousand, tax on it would be about three thousand, six hundred and eighty-nine."
  },
  {
   "id": "L53",
   "file": "vo/L53.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "That's more than she saved in the first place."
  },
  {
   "id": "L54",
   "file": "vo/L54.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Same ten thousand dollars. The only thing that changed is the year it came out."
  },
  {
   "id": "L55",
   "file": "vo/L55.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "So when does an R R S P actually reduce your tax?"
  },
  {
   "id": "L56",
   "file": "vo/L56.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "When your rate on the day you deduct is higher than your rate on the day you withdraw."
  },
  {
   "id": "L57",
   "file": "vo/L57.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "High income now, lower income later: it works. Low income now, higher later: deduct later, or think twice."
  },
  {
   "id": "L58",
   "file": "vo/L58.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Here's your R R S P checklist."
  },
  {
   "id": "L59",
   "file": "vo/L59.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "One. Find your deduction limit on your notice of assessment."
  },
  {
   "id": "L60",
   "file": "vo/L60.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Two. Know your top rate this year, not just your salary."
  },
  {
   "id": "L61",
   "file": "vo/L61.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Three. Low income this year? Contribute if you like, but you can save the deduction for later."
  },
  {
   "id": "L62",
   "file": "vo/L62.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Four. Plan withdrawals for low-income years."
  },
  {
   "id": "L63",
   "file": "vo/L63.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "So, what did we learn?"
  },
  {
   "id": "L64",
   "file": "vo/L64.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "One. An R R S P saves tax at your top rate, not a fixed amount."
  },
  {
   "id": "L65",
   "file": "vo/L65.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Two. You choose when to deduct, and that choice can be worth hundreds of dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L66",
   "file": "vo/L66.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Three. It's a deferral. The tax comes back when the money comes out."
  },
  {
   "id": "L67",
   "file": "vo/L67.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Four. It pays off when your rate today is higher than your rate later."
  },
  {
   "id": "L68",
   "file": "vo/L68.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Next on this channel: capital gains tax in Canada, with a real example. Subscribe, so you don't miss it."
  }
 ],
